on conflict (slug) do nothing;

on conflict (rabbi_id, produce_id) do nothing;

-- Alerts -------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Dates are relative to when this file is run, so the demo always has live
-- alerts and a populated archive.

**What to do**

If you check romaine at home, run the full wash-and-inspect twice rather than once, and expect to find something. If you are not confident, switch to supervised pre-checked lettuce for the rest of the season.

Greenhouse-grown and hydroponic romaine is not affected and is running normally.

This notice will be reviewed at the end of the month.', 'urgent'::alert_severity, 'North America', now() + interval '-6 days', now() + interval '24 days', 'approved', now()),
  ('strawberry-season-opening', 'Local strawberry season is open', 'Peak-season local strawberries carry more than the imported winter supply. Hull and rinse individually.', 'Local strawberries have started arriving. Peak-season fruit consistently runs higher than the imported winter supply, and the difference is large enough to be worth noting.

**What to do**

Hull each berry, taking a thin slice of flesh with the hull, then soak and rinse the berries individually while rubbing the surface. Do not skip the hulling step before soaking — soaking with the hull on traps what you are trying to remove.', 'advisory'::alert_severity, 'North America', now() + interval '-19 days', now() + interval '70 days', 'approved', now()),
  ('dried-goods-storage-reminder', 'Warm-weather reminder: check stored dried goods', 'Storage pests multiply quickly in summer. Go through opened bags of rice, flour and dried fruit.', 'Storage pests breed fastest in warm weather, and an opened bag that was clean in March may not be clean in August.

**What to do**

Go through opened packets of rice, flour, dried fruit and nuts. Spread a sample thinly on a light-coloured tray and look across it for movement, for small beetles, and for grains held together by fine webbing. Anything showing webbing is discarded, along with anything stored touching it.

Moving dried goods to sealed containers in a cool cupboard prevents most of this.', 'info'::alert_severity, 'International', now() + interval '-33 days', now() + interval '45 days', 'approved', now()),
  ('cauliflower-supply-note-winter', 'Winter cauliflower supply running clean', 'This winter''s cauliflower is testing unusually clean, but the checking requirement has not changed.', 'Laboratory sampling of the current winter cauliflower supply has come back cleaner than the seasonal average.

This does not change what is required. A clean batch average does not tell you about the head in your kitchen, and the checking requirement for fresh cauliflower stands unchanged. The note is recorded here because people ask, and because a rumour that ''cauliflower is fine this year'' has been circulating.', 'info'::alert_severity, 'North America', now() + interval '-95 days', now() + interval '-12 days', 'approved', now()),
  ('aphids-uk-iceberg', 'Aphids found deep in UK iceberg lettuce', 'Northern Vaad has raised iceberg lettuce to expert checking for the British supply.', 'Northern Vaad HaKashrus has raised iceberg lettuce from home checking to expert checking for the British supply, following inspections that found aphids well past the outer leaves and into the head.

**What to do**

In the UK, treat iceberg as you would romaine: separate the leaves and inspect each one, or use supervised pre-checked product. Elsewhere the existing guidance is unchanged.', 'advisory'::alert_severity, 'United Kingdom', now() + interval '-41 days', now() + interval '-3 days', 'approved', now())
on conflict (slug) do nothing;

on conflict do nothing;

commit;
